name: Selectable settings, inline editing, drafts and explicit persistence
size: 120x36
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
env-unset: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY KUZUSHI_MODEL KUZUSHI_LANGGRAPH_BRIDGE NODE_OPTIONS NO_COLOR
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/options_browser.py @TMP_TARGET @ART seed @TMP_HOME
require-wrapper-flow:
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | ready
submit: modules
keys: NPage
require-live-snap: 20 selected 3/3 | last-capability
expect: INPUT REQUIRED
keys: NPage
require-live-snap: 20 selected 3/3 | page-stops-at-end
keys: PPage PPage
require-live-snap: 20 selected 1/3 | page-stops-at-start
submit: options context:build
require-live-snap: 20 Sample limit | selected-setting
expect: Value: 200
keys: Enter C-u
type: invalid
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 20 EDIT Sample limit | invalid-value
expect: invalid
expect: save session
ask: Does validation keep the invalid draft in the field and make the correction controls clear?
keys: C-u
type: 7
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 20 Value: 7 | session-saved
expect: session
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/options_browser.py @TMP_TARGET @ART session
keys: Enter C-u
type: 9
keys: C-g
require-live-snap: 20 Saved globally. | globally-saved
expect: Value: 7
expect: session override still applies
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/options_browser.py @TMP_TARGET @ART global
submit: unset sampleLimit
require-live-snap: 20 Value: 9 | global-effective
expect: global
expect-not: session override still applies
nav-mode:
keys: a Down Enter C-u
paste-file: @ART/multiline.txt
require-live-snap: 20 Keep this draft. | multiline-editor
resize: 160x48
require-live-snap: 20 Keep this draft. | editor-160x48
resize: 96x89
require-live-snap: 20 Keep this draft. | editor-96x89
resize: 80x24
require-live-snap: 20 Keep this draft. | editor-80x24
resize: 60x20
require-live-snap: 20 Keep this draft. | editor-60x20
resize: 40x12
require-live-snap: 20 Keep this draft. | editor-40x12
expect: save session
ask: Are the field, cursor and save controls usable across the six sizes, including multiline Unicode text?
resize: 120x36
keys: Escape
require-live-snap: 20 Context prompt | kept-draft
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 20 Operator α | reopened-draft
keys: C-c
require-live-snap: 20 CONFIRM SESSION EXIT | draft-exit-disclosure
expect: tool option drafts
expect-not: Operator α
keys: Escape
require-live-snap: 20 Keep this draft. | stayed-editor
keys: Escape
require-live-snap: 20 Context prompt | returned-browser
submit: show missing threat-model:ask
require-live-snap: 20 Threat model ref | workflow-reference
keys: Enter
live-snap: reference-not-editable
expect: supplied by the workflow
expect-not: EDIT
submit: use codeql
submit: options .
require-live-snap: 20 Module codeql requires an exact tool | exact-tool-required
expect-not: options .` requires a focused module
submit: logs
nav-mode:
keys: z End
require-live-snap: 20 READ TRANSCRIPT | exact-guidance-reader
resize: 160x48
live-snap: guidance-160x48
resize: 96x89
live-snap: guidance-96x89
resize: 80x24
live-snap: guidance-80x24
resize: 60x20
live-snap: guidance-60x20
resize: 40x12
keys: End
live-snap: guidance-40x12
keys: PPage
live-snap: guidance-40x12-previous
ask: Is the focused module's exact-tool requirement and settings path readable through the transcript at all six sizes without implying missing focus or starting work?
keys: q
resize: 120x36
submit: options codeql:scan
require-live-snap: 20 codeql:scan | exact-options-reader
expect: OPTIONS
submit: options x-ray:run
require-live-snap: 20 Experimental | support-120x36
resize: 160x48
require-live-snap: 20 Value: | support-160x48
resize: 96x89
require-live-snap: 20 Value: | support-96x89
resize: 80x24
require-live-snap: 20 Value: | support-80x24
resize: 60x20
require-live-snap: 20 Value: | support-60x20
resize: 40x12
require-live-snap: 20 Value: | support-40x12
expect: Experimental
ask: Can the operator inspect an experimental tool's actual selected setting at every size without starting work?
resize: 120x36
keys: C-c
require-live-snap: 20 CONFIRM SESSION EXIT | kept-draft-exit
keys: y
require-exit: 10
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 NO_COLOR=1
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | restarted
submit: options context:build
require-live-snap: 20 Value: 9 | recovered-global
expect: global
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/options_browser.py @TMP_TARGET @ART restart
ask: Does no-color restart recover only the explicitly global value, with unchanged source and no dispatched jobs?
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
